# cuttle stealth-chromium patch #56 - console previews never run page getters.
#
# Source: chromium 154.0.8037.57 (v8 671f7c27ac04)
#   v8/src/inspector/value-mirror.cc
#   v8/src/inspector/injected-script.cc
#
# Authored for cuttle (issue #50). The paths are inside v8/, a nested git repo
# (a gitlink of build/src); `git apply` run from build/src handles them,
# `git apply --index` would not.
#
# Every driver enables the Runtime domain to get console, exception, binding
# and execution-context events, and from then on V8's inspector builds a
# description and a preview of every console argument and uncaught exception.
# Each page getter that work fires is a read a page can count against a browser
# with no debugger. The #50 probe, a getter on Error.prototype.name around
# console.debug(new Error('')), reads 1 without a debugger and 3 with one
# Runtime-enabled session; each further session adds one (4 in #50 through
# playwright-cli). Measured on Chrome 145 and 151, page and worker alike.
# Upstream's May 2025 guard in getErrorProperty skipped only OWN accessors, so
# the inherited one fired.
#
# The read paths this patch closes, all reached by console/exception previews:
#   1. getErrorProperty (error name, message, stack): walks the chain with
#      GetOwnPropertyDescriptor, returns data values, stops at proxies and page
#      getters, and invokes only builtin getters (as upstream allowed).
#   2. Reading an unformatted error.stack formats it, which Gets and ToStrings
#      name and message on the holder and reads and calls
#      Error.prepareStackTrace - that was the second extra read. The
#      description reads the stack, and the property walk invokes any builtin
#      getter (the stack getter can be installed under any name), only when
#      every level of the chain is inert for name and message and
#      Error.prepareStackTrace is not a function or accessor. V8 reads it off
#      the %Error% of the stack holder's realm, which the public API cannot
#      reach, so every realm on the chain must still have its own builtin Error
#      as the global Error; a replaced or foreign global Error suppresses the
#      stack in the description instead.
#   3. RegExp.prototype.flags, a builtin getter the preview invokes, Gets every
#      flag on its receiver, so a getter on RegExp.prototype.global fired once
#      more per logged regexp. The property walk no longer invokes it.
#   4. Blink "array"-subtype objects (NodeList, HTMLCollection) read length with
#      Get, firing a page getter on NodeList.prototype.length that a debugger-
#      free console never reads.
#   5. console.table's columns array was read with Get after the message text
#      had already read it, firing index getters twice.
#
# Deliberately NOT changed: driver-initiated reads (Runtime.getProperties,
# returnByValue, deep serialization, calling a native getter mirror) - the
# driver asked, as it would in any Chrome. Custom formatters run page code by
# design and only DevTools turns them on. Builtin getters stay trusted, as
# upstream has them; a page installing a builtin that re-enters JS (for example
# Array.prototype.toString) as a getter is not covered.
#
# Not ported: adryfish 001 and clearcote 110 stop addBindings and messageAdded,
# which breaks driver console capture and bindings.
#
# Checked by validate/smoke.py and benches/detect.py (driver-shaped section: the
# probe with Runtime off, then on for the page and an auto-attached worker; the
# counts must not move) and validate/cdp-getter-probe.sh (the bundled driver).
